Package: testudo
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.36), libpam0g, libpam-modules, nftables, iproute2
Recommends: frr, frr-pythontools, keepalived, conntrackd, conntrack, wireguard-tools, kea-dhcp4-server, kea-dhcp6-server, unbound, dns-root-data, chrony, radvd, isc-dhcp-client, dhcpcd-base, ppp, dnsmasq-base, snmpd
Homepage: https://github.com/noahzmr/testudo
Description: firewall, router and network operations console
 Testudo turns a Linux host into a firewall appliance driven by one
 configuration model: packet filter, NAT, routing through FRR, WireGuard,
 a load balancer, intra-site HA with keepalived and conntrackd, and a
 multi-site cluster. Every change is applied atomically and rolled back
 unless confirmed. Flow analysis, replay and alerting run alongside.
